{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPmAgfyjdsB1Ro2ZkwCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #410 to the engineer planner and the engineer worker, with status `done`. The decision is in `.ard/410/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **What it is:** a flaky test, `TestRetryTransportSearchSpacing` (`internal/github/transport_test.go:235`). It times the sixth search from the moment just before that search, so it ignores the tokens that refill while the first five run. On a slow CI machine the wait is correctly shorter than the 60ms the test expects, so the test fails. I read the test and it matches the issue's description. The rate limiter is working as designed.\n- **Why only the engineer:** the fix stays inside one package, with no user-visible change, new interface or stored data. So the product-manager, architect and documentation-planner aren't needed. `engineer` is also the only triage role besides lead in this repository. The `eng-review` reviewer has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it runs on the pull request anyway and I didn't add it.\n- **One thing for a maintainer:** if the planner chooses the issue's preferred fix, driving the limiter at fixed times instead of the real clock, the transport may need a small hook for the test to set the time. That would be a minor code change inside `internal/github`, not only a test edit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":12318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":419,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4a6050c-db88-431b-a8c4-540c409a4fe2","uuid":"ef682d5a-1efc-4a11-8571-9a2ee2965d9d","timestamp":"2026-11-25T13